2247001-14dde9de-25af-4284-ab16-2c57560484f6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented and pushed: Gerrit change 1832 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1832), commit ef97b9ab3f, patchset 1. Single grouped change for dependabot PRs #129 + #130. setup-uv v9.0.0->v10.0.0 across 19 sites / 11 workflow files (0 v9 SHAs remain, 19 v10 SHAs); every use passes enable-cache: true so v10's auto-cache-disable breaking change does not apply. uv.lock: botocore 1.43.70 + json-repair 0.63.1, revision 2->3, mcp stayed 1.29.0, pyproject untouched. NOTE: plain 'uv lock --upgrade-package' resolved PAST the PR (1.43.72 / 0.63.2); re-locked with exact '==' pins to the reviewed versions to stay inside the certified plan scope (newer patches arrive next dependabot round). Gates green: make lint EXIT 0 (ruff+format+complexity ratchet new=0/increased=0+DCO+zizmor+actionlint), make typecheck EXIT 0 (552 files), uv lock --check clean, targeted usage-surface tests 126 passed (test_structured/test_silent_success/test_llm_capabilities/test_usage_log). STOP rule not triggered — everything landed (AC6 vacuous). Both PRs will be commented and left open. Ticket stays in_progress pending LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.","timestamp":1786923926761510001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CLOSE-OUT verified against MERGED origin/main (ef97b9ab3f — Gerrit change 1832 submitted, fast-forward, no rebase). AC1: 19 setup-uv v10 SHAs across 11 workflow files, 0 v9 SHAs remain; all 11 workflows parse. AC2: uv.lock records botocore 1.43.70 + json-repair 0.63.1 (revision 3), mcp still 1.29.0, pyproject unchanged, uv lock --check clean. AC3: make lint + make typecheck green, 126 targeted usage-surface tests passed. AC4: landed via Gerrit as ONE change with rebar-ticket: 5a90-ec98-af5a-48d0 trailer + DCO sign-off (merge implies LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1). AC5: both PR #129 and #130 commented with the grouped change link and now closed. AC6 vacuous — everything landed, STOP rule never triggered. All ACs met; closing.","timestamp":1786925303897286001}],"created_at":1786923380230142001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"480c1e8b-56ee-4707-af77-5dd40b3890c7","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"75fa-3b27-8d94-4a27"}],"description":"# Land dependabot PRs #129 + #130 as ONE Gerrit change (setup-uv v10 + uv-lock botocore/json-repair)\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nGitHub is a read-only mirror: dependabot PRs never merge there; content is\nre-applied locally and landed via Gerrit, then the PRs are commented/closed.\nPer operator directive these two open dependabot PRs are grouped into a SINGLE\nticket and a SINGLE Gerrit change (one commit touching both the CI-action pin\nand the lockfile — the shared \"dependency housekeeping\" lane):\n\n* PR #129 (`dependabot/github_actions/github-actions-fa3bf1173d`, github-actions\n  group): `astral-sh/setup-uv` v9.0.0 (`c771a70e…`) -> v10.0.0 (`ae62891f…`),\n  19 pinned-SHA references across 11 workflow files. VALIDITY: v10 is a major\n  bump; its ONLY breaking change disables the cache for `enable-cache: auto` on\n  `pull_request_target` / `workflow_run` / `release` events (cache-poisoning\n  hardening, astral-sh/setup-uv#984). EVERY rebar usage passes\n  `enable-cache: true` explicitly (never `auto`), so that change does not alter\n  our behavior; the `version`/`version-file` additions are opt-in and unused.\n  Dependabot pins the exact v10.0.0 commit SHA, so the bump is reproducible.\n\n* PR #130 (`dependabot/uv/uv-lock-434831ba27`, uv-lock group): two lock-only\n  patch bumps —\n  - `botocore` 1.43.69 -> 1.43.70 (patch) — SAFE. Routine service-model update;\n    consumed via lazy imports only (`bedrock_model.py`, `structured.py`,\n    `remote_cert.py`). pyproject floor `botocore>=1.43.0` already admits it and\n    boto3's botocore range (`<1.44`) accepts it, so boto3 need not move.\n  - `json-repair` 0.63.0 -> 0.63.1 (patch) — SAFE. `src/rebar/llm/structured.py`\n    calls `repair_json(cand, return_objects=True[, schema=…])`; the called API is\n    unchanged across the patch. Floor `json-repair>=0.61` already admits it.\n  The PR also carries uv's lockfile-format churn: `revision = 2 -> 3` and an\n  httpcore2 marker simplification (dependabot ran a newer uv). Both are\n  format/resolver byproducts, not dependency changes; `uv lock --check` on main\n  already passes latest-uv, so revision is not load-bearing — but we reproduce\n  the PR faithfully by regenerating with a recent uv.\n\n## Approach\n\nIn a fresh worktree branched from `origin/main` (venv on PATH):\n\n1. NO pyproject.toml edit — all bumps are admitted by existing constraints\n   (setup-uv is a SHA pin in workflow YAML, not a pyproject dep; botocore /\n   json-repair floors listed above; no exact pins exist for either).\n2. setup-uv: replace every `astral-sh/setup-uv@c771a70e…  # v9.0.0` with\n   `astral-sh/setup-uv@ae62891fec2bb8e7d6c99fc78c9fec3a63790f8d  # v10.0.0`\n   across the 11 workflow files (19 sites) via an exact-string sed; verify 0\n   remaining v9 SHAs and 19 v10 SHAs.\n3. uv-lock: install a recent uv in the worktree, then\n   `uv lock --upgrade-package botocore --upgrade-package json-repair`. If uv\n   resolves PAST the PR's reviewed versions (per the #128 precedent it did),\n   re-lock with exact `==1.43.70` / `==0.63.1` pins so the landed lock matches\n   the certified scope; the newer patches arrive in the next dependabot round.\n   Then `uv sync --locked --extra dev --extra agents` so gates run against the\n   bumped tree. Verify `git diff uv.lock` moved only botocore/json-repair (plus\n   uv's transitive/format bookkeeping) — no other version churn.\n4. Gates: YAML-parse the 11 changed workflow files; `uv lock --check`;\n   `make lint`; `make typecheck`; targeted usage-surface tests\n   (`pytest tests/unit/test_structured.py tests/unit/test_silent_success.py`\n   for json-repair; `tests/unit/test_llm_capabilities.py` for the botocore lazy\n   import — run whichever exist). Full `pytest tests/unit` is CI's job; CI\n   Verified +1 is the authoritative full-suite gate.\n5. ONE commit (subject <=50 chars, body wrapped at 72) with trailer\n   `rebar-ticket: <this ticket's full canonical id>` + DCO `-s`;\n   `git push gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main`. Leave the ticket in_progress for the\n   bots; the change is submitted only after LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1.\n6. Comment on BOTH PR #129 and PR #130 pointing at the single Gerrit change and\n   noting they were grouped; leave the PRs open for dependabot/operator to close\n   once the mirror updates.\n\n## STOP / defer rule (explicit fallback done-state)\n\nIf a package bump fails its targeted tests or lint/typecheck in step 4: drop\nONLY that package (re-lock from a clean `git checkout uv.lock` with the\nremaining package), record the failure evidence as a ticket comment, and land\nthe remaining safe content. If setup-uv v10 fails a workflow-parse or a real\nusage incompatibility surfaces, drop the actions bump and land the lock subset\n(or vice-versa) — the two halves are independent. The fallback done-state:\nthe ticket closes legitimately with the landed subset, provided every dropped\nitem has a recorded-on-ticket failure reason.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n* Any src/rebar or test code change — nothing in these deltas requires one.\n* boto3 / mcp / any other dependency bump not in PR #129 or #130.\n* pyproject.toml constraint edits and `.github/complexity-baseline.json`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] AC1: on the landed change, all 19 setup-uv references read the v10.0.0 SHA\n  `ae62891fec2bb8e7d6c99fc78c9fec3a63790f8d` across the 11 workflow files, zero\n  v9 SHAs remain, and all 11 changed workflow files still parse as valid YAML.\n- [x] AC2: `uv.lock` records botocore 1.43.70 and json-repair 0.63.1 (or a\n  documented STOP-rule subset), pyproject.toml is unchanged, and\n  `uv lock --check` exits 0.\n- [x] AC3: `make lint` + `make typecheck` exit 0 and the targeted usage-surface\n  tests pass against the bumped tree.\n- [x] AC4: the change lands through Gerrit as a SINGLE change with a\n  `rebar-ticket:` trailer for this ticket's full canonical id + DCO sign-off,\n  after LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1.\n- [x] AC5: both PR #129 and PR #130 carry a comment pointing at the single\n  grouped Gerrit change; both left open for the mirror/dependabot to close.\n- [x] AC6 (fallback): every item dropped under the STOP rule has a ticket\n  comment recording the concrete failure evidence and the re-lock excluding it\n  (vacuously satisfied when everything lands).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml","reason":"setup-uv v9->v10 pinned-SHA bump (3 sites)"},{"path":".github/workflows/_eval-discipline.yml","reason":"setup-uv v9->v10 pinned-SHA bump (1 site)"},{"path":".github/workflows/_mutation.yml","reason":"setup-uv v9->v10 pinned-SHA bump (2 sites)"},{"path":".github/workflows/dependency-advisory-canary.yml","reason":"setup-uv v9->v10 pinned-SHA bump (1 site)"},{"path":".github/workflows/external-integration.yml","reason":"setup-uv v9->v10 pinned-SHA bump (6 sites)"},{"path":".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml","reason":"setup-uv v9->v10 pinned-SHA bump (1 site)"},{"path":".github/workflows/jira-dc-capability-map.yml","reason":"setup-uv v9->v10 pinned-SHA bump (1 site)"},{"path":".github/workflows/prompt-eval.yml","reason":"setup-uv